<Base title="Editorial policy" description="How articles are written, reviewed, corrected and funded on AI Veterinary.">
  <article class="wrap narrow hero prose">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">How content on this site is written, checked, corrected and paid for. Short, because the rules are simple.</p>

    <h2>How an article is made</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Drafting.</strong> Articles are drafted from veterinary guidelines and textbooks (WSAVA, ESCCAP, ISFM, national bodies). Drafting may use AI tools. Every draft is labelled <em>"Draft, awaiting vet review"</em> until a veterinarian has checked it.</li>
      <li><strong>Veterinary review.</strong> A practising veterinarian reads the article, corrects it and signs it. The article then shows the reviewer's name, registration (Ordine, Tierärztekammer or equivalent) and the review date.</li>
      <li><strong>Re-review.</strong> Each reviewed article carries a "next review" date, at most 24 months out. Articles are re-checked earlier when guidelines change.</li>
      <li><strong>References.</strong> Reviewed articles list their sources at the bottom. We prefer guidelines and public health bodies over blogs or product pages.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What we never publish</h2>
    <ul class="paw-list">
      <li>A diagnosis for your animal, or medication doses. Both belong to your veterinarian.</li>
      <li>Claims about a product, brand or clinic in exchange for money, goods or links.</li>
      <li>Content generated by AI and published without a human reading it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If you find an error, write to <a href="mailto:hello@aiveterinary.org">hello@aiveterinary.org</a> with the page link. Factual errors are corrected as soon as a reviewer has confirmed them, usually within a week. The article's "updated" date changes, and material corrections are noted at the bottom of the article. We do not silently rewrite reviewed content.</p>

    <h2>Funding and conflicts of interest</h2>
    <p>AI Veterinary is an independent side project of its founder and is currently funded by nobody: there is no advertising, no sponsorship and no affiliate link on this site. Should that change, each sponsored or affiliate element will be labelled on the page where it appears, and this policy will be updated first.</p>
    <p>Reviewing veterinarians declare relevant ties (employment, consulting, shareholdings in animal-health companies) before reviewing. A reviewer with a tie to a product does not review articles about that product class.</p>

    <h2>AI on this site</h2>
    <p>AI tools help draft articles and translations and power the documentation assistant for vets. Where AI produced or helped produce something you read, we say so. A veterinarian, not software, has the last word on every reviewed article and every clinical document.</p>

    <p><a href="/about">About the project</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
